=Write a short follow-up email from a recruiter to a past candidate who has not replied to an email about a job opening.

Recruiter: {{ $json.recruiter_name }} at {{ $json.agency }}
Candidate first name: {{ $json.first_name }}
Job details: {{ $json.job_summary }}
This is follow-up {{ $json.followup_number }} of {{ $json.total_followups }}. Final follow-up: {{ $json.is_final }}

Rules:
- 40 to 80 words, friendly and low-pressure, plain text.
- If this is not the final follow-up: a short check-in that mentions one detail from the job details above.
- If this is the final follow-up: politely close the loop and say they can reply any time if their situation changes.
- Only use facts given above. Do not invent pay, benefits, dates or other details.
- Do not repeat the whole original email. Do not mention AI or automation.
- Sign off with the recruiter's first name and the agency name.

Reply with JSON only, no other text:
{"body": "<email body, use \n for line breaks>"}

